uuid "b280d9a7-460b-53f4-950e-5c4db54798ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-87876" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-4-{e}^{3x}>2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4-{e}^{3x} & >2 \\\\ -{e}^{3x} & >6 \\\\ {e}^{3x} & <-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $e>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nTherefore, ${e}^{3x}$ cannot be less than $-6.$ Hence, the inequality\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x}<-6\n$$\n\nhas no solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a114450f-bfcd-5db3-9060-fcd067c606fa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" :answer/id #uuid "c41bfc32-367b-5f7b-ad16-a7f74b36a678" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "no solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" :answer/id #uuid "8aff37d3-2b04-5246-94e0-3cb18b29d63d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection/42a9bdfe075ad1cd1cd1aff86215f59abad9e2705a4a6069984e77ec646a92d7" :answer/id #uuid "7f3bac30-6f27-5e01-900f-93af7ebb1b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<1-{log}_{15/4}⁡(9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection/d8a167b2f86a18fa284aefe264ef0c35a0b3166154d86d12836cbd880463df6c" :answer/id #uuid "b51e59dc-b463-539a-833d-11e02970e132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection/c9f503d2289873e2852b653f2e282532bc8e4caec9a460dc28751def8d9a8bb2" :answer/id #uuid "98f88f13-96fc-5ebc-94f5-b5fe5a4b853f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d7ce77-d77b-54f4-865d-0d8e114b1c9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87891/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" :answer-field/choices ["q-87891/selection/52f8bfd00f6b3deb0e93232df027641f8c16cee0e37ff5f896dd75bd009234e2" "q-87891/selection/12cf5bf844cf95b95e80f529266ac6af4ed60a8ea790e2b44db6283719be635c" "q-87891/selection/42a9bdfe075ad1cd1cd1aff86215f59abad9e2705a4a6069984e77ec646a92d7" "q-87891/selection/d8a167b2f86a18fa284aefe264ef0c35a0b3166154d86d12836cbd880463df6c" "q-87891/selection/c9f503d2289873e2852b653f2e282532bc8e4caec9a460dc28751def8d9a8bb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87891" :question/id #uuid "da4d4661-f1df-587e-b77b-1ec068db7274" :question/math-academy-id "q-87891" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3\\cdot {(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x}+27>0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x}+27 & >0 \\\\ 3\\cdot {(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x} & >-27 \\\\ {(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x} & >-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $\\frac{15}{4}>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nIn particular, every value of ${(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x}$ is greater than $-9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{15}{4})}^{1-x}>-9\n$$\n\nfor all real values of $x.$\n\nHence, the original inequality is satisfied for all real numbers." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87891/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a114450f-bfcd-5db3-9060-fcd067c606fa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87895/selection/4abc2edc39532b0da014f35f904ebb7f4efad6933be